        "content": "<p>Most pointwise instances on <code>Set</code> such as <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.mul#doc\">docs#Set.mul</a> are scoped to the <code>Pointwise</code> namespace . An exception to this is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.instInvolutiveStar#doc\">docs#Set.instInvolutiveStar</a>, which causes some awkwardness in CSLib currently. Is this something accidental where a PR would be welcome?</p>",
        "id": 633688958,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1792597128
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(I think this would apply to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.involutiveInv#doc\">docs#Set.involutiveInv</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.involutiveNeg#doc\">docs#Set.involutiveNeg</a> as well)</p>",
